%[text] - What happens to the poles when $c = 2${"altText":"c = 2"}? Physically, what does this represent?
%[text] - If any of the parameters are (individually) negative, what happens to the poles? What are the physical implications of negative parameters?
%[text] - As $k${"altText":"k"} is increased, what happens to the poles? How does this relate to the natural frequency expression that you solved for in part **(a)** ($\\omega\_n = \\sqrt{k/m}${"altText":"\omega\_n = \sqrt{k\/m}"})? \
